<Page title="Credits & Open-Source Licenses — EditableFrames" description="Credits for the original EditableFrames creative studies, MIT framework code, Three.js rendering library, and the fonts used in this browser playground." path="/credits/">
<article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">MADE WITH OPEN TOOLS</p><h1>Good work<br/><em>has good company.</em></h1><h2>Original studies and framework</h2><p>The twelve studies are code-generated scenes created for the EditableFrames project. They explore procedural 3D, scientific illustration, isometric systems, paper and ink animation, grain, and kinetic typography. Public creative-coding experiments informed the research; their videos, screenshots and source were not copied into these scenes. No endorsement by referenced creators is implied.</p><p>The framework code and original scene code are distributed under the <a href="/LICENSE.txt">MIT license</a>. A pinned subset of EditableFrames beta 0.1.0 powers this playground. Hosted study code is curated; this website does not run arbitrary user-submitted code.</p><h2>Rendering and website</h2><p>3D studies use <a href="https://threejs.org/">Three.js</a>, under its <a href="/THREE-LICENSE.txt">MIT license</a>. Canvas draws the illustrated studies. The site uses Astro and React, with <a href="/BRICOLAGE-OFL.txt">Bricolage Grotesque</a> and <a href="/IBM-PLEX-OFL.txt">IBM Plex Mono</a> fonts under the SIL Open Font License.</p><p>Procedural castle, dragon and railway geometry is built in code. The product study includes three separately licensed phone models; their geometry was authored by the artists credited below. A scientific U-Net illustration shows a visual metaphor, not neural-model execution or measured results.</p><h2>Device models and studio lighting</h2><p><a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/iphone-17-pro-4541aa8a28324b33a2baaf81d263aaec">iPhone 17 Pro by Ranguel</a> is licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>, distributed through app-preview-craft. <a href="https://github.com/CodyJasonBennett/device-models">iPhone 12 and Pixel 6 by Cody Bennett</a> use the <a href="/devices/CODY-MIT.txt">MIT license</a>. Runtime files were decoded for browser use. We replace display materials with a fictional animated app and apply an aluminum material approximation on the iPhone 17 Pro; the original GLB geometry and body textures remain.</p><p><a href="https://polyhaven.com/a/studio_small_09">Studio Small 09 by Sergej Majboroda / Poly Haven</a> provides the HDR environment under CC0. Lighting is an artistic studio treatment, not a measured manufacturer color reference. No endorsement by Apple, Google or the artists is implied. <a href="/devices/ATTRIBUTIONS.txt">Full attributions</a> · <a href="/devices/manifest.json">Asset sources and hashes</a>.</p><h2>Tool logos</h2><p>Claude, OpenAI, Grok, Codex and GitHub SVG marks are supplied by <a href="https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons">Lobe Icons</a> under its <a href="/LOBE-ICONS-LICENSE.txt">MIT license</a>. Product names and marks belong to their respective owners and identify the tools in the setup guide; no endorsement is implied.</p><h2>Privacy of your edits</h2><p>Your settings stay in browser storage on this device. The playground sends no scene edits to a server, requires no account and requests no camera or microphone access. Static page and asset requests are delivered through Cloudflare. Downloads are generated in your browser.</p><p><a href="/guide/">Read the playground guide</a> or <a href="/#gallery">explore the collection</a>.</p></article>
